Subject: [PATCH] Input: ff-memless - stop an effect that was updated while playing

Uploading new parameters for a playing effect clears FF_EFFECT_PLAYING and leaves the
change to the timer. A stop that comes before the timer runs then finds the effect not
playing, clears FF_EFFECT_STARTED and never tells the driver, so the device keeps the
last level it was given. With pwm-vibrator, a game that changed its rumble every frame
left the motor running for good, also after it closed the device.

Abort every started effect instead, so the next combination reaches the driver; for one
that never played it is a harmless update without it.
---
--- a/drivers/input/ff-memless.c
+++ b/drivers/input/ff-memless.c
@@ -447,10 +447,12 @@
 	} else {
 		pr_debug("initiated stop\n");
 
-		if (test_bit(FF_EFFECT_PLAYING, &state->flags))
+		/*
+		 * An upload clears FF_EFFECT_PLAYING of a playing effect until the timer
+		 * runs, so a started effect may be playing on the device without it.
+		 */
+		if (test_bit(FF_EFFECT_STARTED, &state->flags))
 			__set_bit(FF_EFFECT_ABORTING, &state->flags);
-		else
-			__clear_bit(FF_EFFECT_STARTED, &state->flags);
 	}
 
 	ml_play_effects(ml);
